Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.91,0:00:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Yamoo! Yamoo! Yamoo! Yamoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.39,0:00:31.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.63,0:01:06.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Take a look, Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.67,0:01:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The seal of Orakalko surrounds us,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.79,0:01:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,strengthening my obelisk, while your\Nmonsters stand powerless in his shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.89,0:01:20.47,Default,,0,0,0,,First you lose them,\Nthen you lose your soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.95,0:01:31.47,Default,,0,0,0,,All at the hands of your own creature
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.25,0:01:35.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Who knew the very card that\Nbrought you so much glory.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.87,0:01:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Would lead to your downfall\NAnd it all begins right now
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.89,0:01:44.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk the Tormentor attack
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.69,0:01:46.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Fist of fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.63,0:01:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.57,0:01:59.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, it'll take more than that to\Nkeep my pal down, you freak show.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.85,0:02:01.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.76,0:02:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,there's not a card in your deck that can\Nmatch the unparalleled strength of Obelisk.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.03,0:02:07.86,Default,,0,0,0,,He's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.94,0:02:11.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk is stronger than ever thanks\Nto that Ori Kalkos magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.57,0:02:22.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like someone needs a rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.95,0:02:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,The boss warned us that\Nthe Egyptian god cards and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.83,0:02:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,the magic of the Aurichalcos\Nmight not mix so well,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.61,0:02:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,didn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.52,0:02:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I think that geezer's just\Ngetting too old for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.77,0:02:36.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's why we made\Nhim duel first, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.51,0:02:38.33,Default,,0,0,0,,To test the pharaoh's strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.05,0:02:41.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I have an idea that just might work.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.93,0:02:46.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I play the magic\Ncard graceful charity.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.45,0:02:57.47,Default,,0,0,0,,This lets me draw three\Ncards as long as I discard.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.55,0:03:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,two excellent there may\Nbe hope for me after all
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.13,0:03:06.03,Default,,0,0,0,,first i'll summon gazelle\Nthe king of mythical
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.11,0:03:09.39,Default,,0,0,0,,beasts then i'll place\None card face down on the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.99,0:03:11.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That ends my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.61,0:03:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Where was I?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.29,0:03:17.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.55,0:03:21.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I was just about to attack you\Nagain with Obelisk the Tormentor!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.03,0:03:29.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Aw, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.53,0:03:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Now Yugi's got no monsters on the\Nfield to protect his life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.57,0:03:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Tharo, the age of destruction is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.47,0:03:38.82,Default,,0,0,0,,The earth shall be shrouded in darkness.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.19,0:03:43.23,Default,,0,0,0,,And your very soul shall fuel the\Nforce that devastates mankind.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.95,0:03:45.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean by that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.43,0:03:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,A great beast is now\Nawakening from its ancient
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.71,0:03:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,slumber to complete what\Nit began centuries ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.03,0:03:56.62,Default,,0,0,0,,But before this beast can arise,\Nit must absorb enough souls.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.73,0:03:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,That sounds oddly familiar.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.51,0:04:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, where did we hear that\Ncreepy mumbo-jumbo before?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.91,0:04:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The ancient destruction is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.31,0:04:09.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Soon, your souls will be\Noffered to the great beast.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.91,0:04:10.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.95,0:04:13.93,Default,,0,0,0,,And how do you know these\Nevents will come to pass?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.01,0:04:16.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone's got an awful lot of questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.63,0:04:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, it's those biker punks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.25,0:04:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Who do you guys think you are?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.59,0:04:23.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Haven't you been paying attention?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.69,0:04:25.17,Default,,0,0,0,,We're soul collectors.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.73,0:04:30.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Matter of fact, I've got two\Nunfortunate souls right here in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.45,0:04:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,They can trap people's\Nspirits inside cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.25,0:04:37.72,Default,,0,0,0,,That's exactly what Pegasus did to Kaiba\Nand Mokuba with his Millennium Eye!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.91,0:04:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,How do these guys have that kind of power?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.33,0:04:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The sooner you make your next move,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.77,0:04:50.01,Default,,0,0,0,,the sooner Obelisk the Tormentor can\Nstomp out the rest of your life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.09,0:04:54.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk is powerful but not\Nunbeatable, and I intend to prove it!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.49,0:04:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That card belongs to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.55,0:05:01.01,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'm quite familiar with its\Nstrengths and its weaknesses!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.09,0:05:01.97,Default,,0,0,0,,What weaknesses?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.05,0:05:08.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll show you by activating Monster\NReborn in order to bring back Valkyra,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.77,0:05:10.03,Default,,0,0,0,,the Magna Warrior!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.85,0:05:13.01,Default,,0,0,0,,That card?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.45,0:05:14.92,Default,,0,0,0,,In case you've forgotten,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.07,0:05:18.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk already crushed your\NValkyra earlier in the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.85,0:05:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, but I've decided to give my\NMagna Warrior a second chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.19,0:05:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,So say goodbye to your God card.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.23,0:05:28.15,Default,,0,0,0,,But my monster is clearly\Nstronger than yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.23,0:05:31.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps, but you've forgotten one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.45,0:05:33.80,Default,,0,0,0,,My beast is made up of several monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.07,0:05:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Valkyra, disassemble!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.89,0:05:47.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I have one more card to activate.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.45,0:05:51.99,Default,,0,0,0,,The magic card Brave Attack,\Nsending my warriors into battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.59,0:05:53.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Alpha, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.23,0:06:00.61,Default,,0,0,0,,That's all? No! Beta, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.53,0:06:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Your monsters can't even\Nscratch my Egyptian god.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.97,0:06:09.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you need to take\Na closer look because I
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.69,0:06:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,see a rather large scratch\Nacross your Egyptian god.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.57,0:06:14.40,Default,,0,0,0,,But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.61,0:06:19.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Your puny magnet warriors are nothing\Ncompared to the divine strength of my obelisk.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.77,0:06:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But I played my brave\Nattack card. Therefore,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.97,0:06:25.09,Default,,0,0,0,,the damage from each one of my monsters'
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.17,0:06:31.07,Default,,0,0,0,,attacks gets added together, enabling them\Nto bring down Obelisk as a team. Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.31,0:06:32.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.41,0:06:37.47,Default,,0,0,0,,His Alpha's got 1,400 attack\Npoints, plus 1,700 from his Beta.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.79,0:06:38.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't hurt yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.25,0:06:42.15,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a total of 3,100\Nattack points so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.33,0:06:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Obelisk has a strength of 4,500,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.75,0:06:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,so I need 1,500 more points to beat him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.19,0:06:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's exactly what I have left.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.73,0:06:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Gamma!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.99,0:06:55.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy Obelisk now!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.01,0:07:14.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It worked! Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.49,0:07:16.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Way to show him who's boss, Hugh!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.49,0:07:17.63,Default,,0,0,0,,So he got lucky.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.97,0:07:21.75,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll need more than luck to\Nbreak the seal of Oricalkos.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.01,0:07:23.53,Default,,0,0,0,,You can say that again.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.29,0:07:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel's far from done.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.41,0:07:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't need Obelisk to crush you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.17,0:07:34.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I've got all the power I need to\Nwin this duel here in my deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.35,0:07:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll draw them out\Nwith Card of Sanctity.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.45,0:07:38.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.36,0:07:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,That allows me to draw more\Ncards as well. That's cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.81,0:07:43.28,Default,,0,0,0,,They both have six cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.45,0:07:44.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Now they're even.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.71,0:07:49.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Not really, cause that guy's still got\Nhis weird magic circle on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.09,0:07:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,which gives his monsters\Nan instant power boost.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.69,0:07:53.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I play Waterpond!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.23,0:07:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,It's still my turn!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.65,0:07:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm aware of that,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.39,0:08:01.15,Default,,0,0,0,,but Waterpond's special\Nability allows me to
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.23,0:08:04.87,Default,,0,0,0,,automatically summon it to the\Nfield as soon as I draw it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.57,0:08:08.71,Default,,0,0,0,,That card's useless anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.93,0:08:13.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Unlike this, I worry a die, Garetha!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.73,0:08:17.83,Default,,0,0,0,,And thanks to the Orakalkos,\Nhe gains 500 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.79,0:08:21.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You've activated my trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.81,0:08:23.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Behold, Dark Renewal!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.35,0:08:26.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to this card,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.11,0:08:31.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I now have the ability to sacrifice one\Nof your monsters in addition to mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.25,0:08:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I can bring a Spellcaster back from my\Ngraveyard, and I choose my Dark Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.63,0:08:50.57,Default,,0,0,0,,But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.83,0:08:53.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This must be some sort\Nof trick I never sent
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.51,0:08:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,your dark magician to\Nthe card graveyard No,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.49,0:08:59.99,Default,,0,0,0,,but I did when I played my\Ngraceful charity magic card
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.07,0:09:03.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Now he's back and you have\Nno monsters to protect you
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.67,0:09:07.29,Default,,0,0,0,,This face down card is all I need
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.33,0:09:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah, Yugi's gonna clean\Nhouse now. You're done.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.85,0:09:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.93,0:09:16.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.29,0:09:19.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Wipe out his life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.47,0:09:21.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Activate Shield Wall!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.15,0:09:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.41,0:09:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It's quite a handy magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.09,0:09:31.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Shield Wall reinforces my\Ndefense with four new monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.65,0:09:35.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Dark Magician will never\Nget to my life points. No!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.17,0:09:38.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid so,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.87,0:09:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,but just to make sure I think\NI'll summon a few more monsters to
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.59,0:09:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,The field now. By utilizing the power\Nof my Bronze Knight's magic card
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.37,0:09:52.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I discard three cards\Nfrom my hand in order
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.85,0:09:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,to summon three bronze\Nknights to the field
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.07,0:09:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, you have six monsters
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.89,0:10:02.27,Default,,0,0,0,,That's cheating, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.53,0:10:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,check the rules Page three of\Nthe Duelist Handbook clearly
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.21,0:10:10.47,Default,,0,0,0,,states only five monsters per\Nduelist can be in play at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.65,0:10:15.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You better get yourself a new rulebook,\N'cause it sounds like yours is outdated.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.97,0:10:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The seal of Oricalcos\Ndoubles the number of
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.95,0:10:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,monsters its holder is\Nallowed to have on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.21,0:10:24.04,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.12,0:10:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,That means this creepazoid can have up to\Nten monsters in play at one time. Correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.73,0:10:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And you can't attack\Nmy back row of monsters
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.25,0:10:36.11,Default,,0,0,0,,without first going through\Nthe front row. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.41,0:10:41.31,Default,,0,0,0,,And since every one of my monsters\Ngains 500 extra attack points,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.41,0:10:43.06,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll never take them down.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.53,0:10:50.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Your lone dark magician is nothing\Ncompared to my army of creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.47,0:10:52.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Say farewell to your soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.93,0:11:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,The ancient magic that encircles us\Naffords me powers you could never dream of!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.13,0:11:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my move.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.93,0:11:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,so I place two cards face down and\Nsummon Queen's Knight in defense mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.23,0:11:11.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well, now watch this!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.81,0:11:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not finished just yet! What?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.49,0:11:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Dust Tornado!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.47,0:11:21.73,Default,,0,0,0,,This great storm can wipe out\Nany magic or trap card I choose!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.81,0:11:27.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Dust Tornado, eliminate his Seal\Nof Orichalcos with your mighty winds!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.37,0:11:32.43,Default,,0,0,0,,All red eyes won't be so\Ntough when this blows over!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.07,0:11:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodbye, Seal of Orichalcos!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.93,0:11:39.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh no!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.29,0:11:41.59,Default,,0,0,0,,It wasn't destroyed!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.03,0:11:44.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Doesn't he realize the\Nsacred seal is way too
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.55,0:11:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,powerful to be broken\Nby a measly trap card?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.49,0:11:49.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess he's a slow learner!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.27,0:11:51.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, take this!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.41,0:11:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It's called the Warrior Returning Alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.71,0:11:58.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It brings back my lost\Nsoldier, Die Grappa!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.83,0:12:05.65,Default,,0,0,0,,And like every one of my monsters, the\NSeal of Arakalkos raises his strength!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.61,0:12:10.65,Default,,0,0,0,,But wait, there's more!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.97,0:12:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,The magic of allied forces!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.27,0:12:18.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Not only does this card grant my new\Nsoldier an extra 800 attack points,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.55,0:12:22.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It increases the power of my\Nthree Bronze Knights as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.89,0:12:28.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Farewell!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.09,0:12:32.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Warrior Diagrepha,\Ndestroy his Dark Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.99,0:12:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Bronze Knight, eradicate his final\Nmonster with Medieval Sword Slash!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.47,0:12:42.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Queen's Knight, escape!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.09,0:12:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,She's gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.85,0:12:46.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.76,0:12:48.57,Default,,0,0,0,,my face-down card, Magical Academy,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.83,0:12:52.07,Default,,0,0,0,,allowed me to replace her\Nwith my Dark Magician Girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.33,0:12:54.65,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not fair!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.95,0:12:58.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to my Magic card,\Nit's quite fair. And now,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.65,0:13:01.13,Default,,0,0,0,,my Dark Magician Girl shall rid the field
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.21,0:13:06.03,Default,,0,0,0,,of all your monsters and lead me\Nto victory! It's over! Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.27,0:13:08.86,Default,,0,0,0,,And just how will one\Nmonster destroy seven?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.05,0:13:13.53,Default,,0,0,0,,First, she'll receive 300 attack points\Nthanks to the Dark Magician in my graveyard!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.61,0:13:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Your little girl will need more than a few\Nextra points to stand up to my warriors.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.09,0:13:20.86,Default,,0,0,0,,She's a bit out of her league.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.43,0:13:26.90,Default,,0,0,0,,There's one card in my deck that can\Nchange that, but I have to draw it now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.43,0:13:29.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, heart of the cards, guide me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.77,0:13:36.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.27,0:13:39.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I activate this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.41,0:13:41.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Diffusion wave motion.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.05,0:13:43.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.03,0:13:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You're kidding me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.51,0:13:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Talk about luck of the draw, mate!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.97,0:13:51.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And now...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.33,0:13:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Dark Magician Girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.51,0:13:58.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy every one of his monsters\Nwith Dark Burning Attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.25,0:14:08.29,Default,,0,0,0,,The more monsters you have,\Nthe more life points you lose!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.73,0:14:09.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I lost!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.99,0:14:14.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.91,0:14:16.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, he just won.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.15,0:14:18.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Hand me those cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.65,0:14:19.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, never.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.97,0:14:23.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The Egyptian god cards\Nare ours. We had a deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.83,0:14:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, take obelisk.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.91,0:14:30.73,Default,,0,0,0,,No, this wasn't supposed to happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.29,0:14:32.12,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.55,0:14:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Please spare me, master.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.19,0:14:40.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.07,0:14:42.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, it's his own fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.25,0:14:46.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I always thought the old man\Nwas cramping our style anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.47,0:14:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Besides, now we know more about\NYugi's dueling strategies.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.67,0:14:52.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, now let's go. Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.43,0:14:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me back the god cards!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.03,0:14:59.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, you didn't hold up\Nyour end of the deal, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.57,0:15:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to beat all of\Nus, not just one of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.31,0:15:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,But I'll tell you what, this\Nis for being such a good sport.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.17,0:15:13.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.21,0:15:16.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Rex Raptor and Weevil Underwood
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.73,0:15:22.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I released your friend's souls as\Na gift. I'll give you a gift. Just
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.61,0:15:26.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Come down here and get it. It's the\Ngift that keeps on giving again and
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.87,0:15:32.25,Default,,0,0,0,,again That one's got spunk He\Nreminds me of myself Only dumber and
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.33,0:15:37.23,Default,,0,0,0,,not nearly as attractive Toying with\Nthat guy's gonna be fun Come on,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.31,0:15:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,fellas Hey,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.71,0:15:40.30,Default,,0,0,0,,don't turn your back on me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.71,0:15:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, be careful, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.07,0:15:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think that guy's\Ngetting up anytime soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.07,0:15:50.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a bad feeling about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.33,0:15:53.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.61,0:15:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,When he lost our duel, his\Nsoul was trapped in this card.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.79,0:16:00.53,Default,,0,0,0,,But where does this power come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.85,0:16:02.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Check this out, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.61,0:16:05.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It was around that guy's neck.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.69,0:16:08.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you think it has something\Nto do with all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.97,0:16:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Take your paws off me, you Sasquatch!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.71,0:16:17.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, don't make me get\Nall ninja on your butt.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.15,0:16:18.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I got an idea, dude.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.05,0:16:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,See how far we can toss these dweebs?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.51,0:16:22.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on a second, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.01,0:16:25.36,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta find out what happened to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.81,0:16:29.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, now try to remember\Neverything you guys did yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.31,0:16:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I woke up and went to the bathroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.85,0:16:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,He means after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.63,0:16:35.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Ever hear a stepping aside?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.27,0:16:36.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, what's your problem?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.07,0:16:41.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The problem shall be yours when I\Nstrip you two fools of your souls.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.35,0:16:45.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Does the Grim Reaper know\Nyou raided as Wardrobe?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.01,0:16:48.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Ward Valadecu Vestrum Animus.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.43,0:16:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I just think you just got it bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.61,0:16:54.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Rise to your feet and duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.99,0:16:57.59,Default,,0,0,0,,After that, we all duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.81,0:17:00.16,Default,,0,0,0,,And he squashed Weevil like a cockroach.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.33,0:17:02.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Rex was holding us back.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.97,0:17:07.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I would have won, but the guy played some\Nweird card called the Seal of Something.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.97,0:17:09.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The Seal of Ori Kalkos?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.97,0:17:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.67,0:17:14.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And I thought it was one of\Nthose fake knockoff cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.69,0:17:16.65,Default,,0,0,0,,He didn't happen to mention anything about
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.73,0:17:19.38,Default,,0,0,0,,a plan to steal the\Nthree Egyptian god cards,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.47,0:17:20.30,Default,,0,0,0,,did he?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.38,0:17:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, they're gone?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.29,0:17:22.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He took them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.23,0:17:26.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, he and his gang of\Nthugs did. No way! Seriously?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.67,0:17:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Seriously.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.61,0:17:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, we'll win him back one, two, three.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.71,0:17:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,And you two better tell us if you see\Nthree suspicious-looking biker punks,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.81,0:17:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,all right? Sure we will.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.45,0:17:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll be the first to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.45,0:17:42.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Or not. All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.07,0:17:45.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The three Egyptian god\Ncards are up for grabs.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.27,0:17:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Soon they'll be all mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.63,0:17:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.25,0:17:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,First things got freaky at the museum.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.77,0:17:55.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Then monsters started\Nappearing around the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.99,0:18:00.64,Default,,0,0,0,,and now a gang of bikers are stealing\Npeople's souls with a Duel Monsters card.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.89,0:18:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm thinking all those things have\Nsomething to do with one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.53,0:18:05.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, really?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.45,0:18:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm thinking, why does all this\Nweird stuff always happen to us?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.51,0:18:11.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You gotta admit, it's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.53,0:18:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.99,0:18:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been looking all over for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.45,0:18:17.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.36,0:18:18.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, hi, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.85,0:18:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.01,0:18:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you forgot about me now\Nthat you're a big-time champion duelist!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.61,0:18:28.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, do you have any idea\Nwho this is? Let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.21,0:18:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,This card should ring a bell.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.25,0:18:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You did give it to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.71,0:18:37.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebecca!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.62,0:18:38.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to have this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.93,0:18:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,That tie's a friendship.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.37,0:18:43.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Consider it a gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.95,0:18:45.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Aw, thank you. Aw, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.35,0:18:47.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You're that brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.33,0:18:50.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.59,0:18:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You look different.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.85,0:18:53.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you get a haircut or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.27,0:18:55.75,Default,,0,0,0,,No, she traded her teddy bear for glasses.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.65,0:18:58.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't need a teddy bear.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.55,0:19:01.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Because now I have a\Nboyfriend to protect me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.29,0:19:04.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, a boyfriend?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.99,0:19:07.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And yet another weird\Nevent to add to the list.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.29,0:19:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep, and this one tops them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.91,0:19:13.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Probably best if we stay out of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.29,0:19:17.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, my grandpa really\Nwants to see you also, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.41,0:19:19.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Professor Hawkins wants to see me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.05,0:19:23.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Remarkable, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.27,0:19:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,That's my boy. Hey, guys!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.05,0:19:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Yukimoto!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.25,0:19:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just the person I need to see.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.93,0:19:35.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a theory that all of these monster\Nsightings have something to do with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.61,0:19:44.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we are, gang.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.19,0:19:46.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Home, sweet home.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.97,0:19:49.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait till the boss hears\Nwe found the Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.87,0:20:25.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
